    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (50/50 passing, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary of changes\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic over `(lastName, postcode)` and rewired everything that keys off the household to use it.\n\n**`util/Households.java`** \u2014 `householdId(lastName, address)` \u2192 `householdId(lastName, postcode)`, now returning the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalize(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode)`. Updated the class/method docs accordingly. `normalize` and `identityKey` are unchanged, so `identityKey` automatically picks up the new household value.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `householdId` and `identityKey` MapStruct expressions now pass `owner.getPostcode()` instead of `owner.getAddress()`, so the returned DTO fields reflect the computed household.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Reads the request-only `sharesHousehold` flag.\n- Added `rejectDuplicateHousehold(owner, sharesHousehold)` (after the identity check): when an existing owner already shares the computed `householdId`, it throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is set, which bypasses the block and creates the owner as a declared member. Owners without a postcode are never treated as household duplicates (preserving prior soft-match semantics).\n- `countHouseholdMembers` now keys off `(lastName, postcode)`, so the `householdSize` fed into membership derivation uses the same computed id.\n- A declared household member is **not** flagged: `possibleDuplicateOf` is forced to `null` (so `possibleDuplicate=false`) whenever `sharesHousehold` is set.\n- The duplicate-identity exception message now builds its `householdId` from the postcode.\n- Imported `DuplicateHouseholdException` (its 409 handler was already wired in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`).\n\nThis satisfies the new checkpoints: same lastName+postcode share one `householdId` (Cp11/Cp36); a second such owner is a 409 unless it declares `sharesHousehold` (Cp10/Cp35), in which case it's created and not flagged (Cp35); and identity/household-based duplicate detection all key off the computed id (Cp03/Cp25/Cp28/Cp23).",
